IMPORT prelude

-- M4 (spec §10): `LIST OF` as a docassemble `DAList` gather.
--
-- The rule is a household eligibility test over a list the interview must
-- GATHER: how many tenants there are is not known until the user says so, and
-- each tenant carries its own questions.
--
-- Two claims ride on this file, and both are why the backend is worth having:
--
--   * PER-ELEMENT SHORT-CIRCUIT. `the tenant qualifies` is `age AT LEAST 18
--     AND signed`, so for a tenant aged 17 the SIGNING question must never be
--     asked — of that tenant. Docassemble prunes per element inside a gather
--     (probed against 1.10.7), so this is a property the target can actually
--     honour, not an aspiration.
--   * CROSS-COMBINATOR SHORT-CIRCUIT. When `all …` is already FALSE the
--     `any … has been evicted` conjunct decides nothing, so no eviction
--     question may be asked at all.
--
-- The empty household is deliberate, not an oversight: `all` over no tenants
-- is vacuously TRUE and `any` over no tenants is vacuously FALSE, so a
-- household with no named tenant is "eligible". That is a real drafting bug in
-- the rule as written, and the zero-element #EVAL pins it so the gather cannot
-- quietly paper over it.

DECLARE Tenant
    HAS
      @desc Age of this tenant, in whole years, at the start of the tenancy
      age IS A NUMBER
      @desc Whether this tenant signed the tenancy agreement
      `signed the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      @desc Whether this tenant has been evicted from a social tenancy before
      `has been evicted` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE Household
    HAS
      @desc Every tenant named on the tenancy agreement
      tenants IS A LIST OF Tenant

GIVEN t IS A Tenant @desc A tenant named on the agreement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the tenant qualifies` t IF
        t's age AT LEAST 18
    AND t's `signed the agreement`

@export Whether the household qualifies for the tenancy
GIVEN h IS A Household @desc The household applying for the tenancy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the household is eligible` h IF
        all (GIVEN t YIELD `the tenant qualifies` t) (h's tenants)
    AND NOT (any (GIVEN t YIELD t's `has been evicted`) (h's tenants))

-- Two adult signatories, neither previously evicted.
#EVAL `the household is eligible` OF
        Household
        WITH
            tenants IS
                LIST  (Tenant WITH age IS 30, `signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `has been evicted` IS FALSE)
                    , (Tenant WITH age IS 25, `signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `has been evicted` IS FALSE)
-- TRUE

-- The first tenant is a minor. `all` fails on element 0, so nothing about
-- element 0's signature, nothing about element 1 at all, and nothing about
-- eviction, decides anything.
#EVAL `the household is eligible` OF
        Household
        WITH
            tenants IS
                LIST  (Tenant WITH age IS 17, `signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `has been evicted` IS FALSE)
                    , (Tenant WITH age IS 25, `signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `has been evicted` IS FALSE)
-- FALSE

-- Both adults and both signed, but the second has been evicted before.
#EVAL `the household is eligible` OF
        Household
        WITH
            tenants IS
                LIST  (Tenant WITH age IS 30, `signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `has been evicted` IS FALSE)
                    , (Tenant WITH age IS 25, `signed the agreement` IS TRUE, `has been evicted` IS TRUE)
-- FALSE

-- The empty household: vacuously eligible. See the header.
#EVAL `the household is eligible` OF Household WITH tenants IS LIST
-- TRUE
